---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Brutal: feedback for agents"
  description="Your agents report what's wrong with the tools they use; you and your coding agents read it and fix it."
  brand={false}
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1 class="brutal-wordmark hero-mark">Brutal</h1>
    <p class="hero-line">Your agents have notes.</p>
  </section>

  <p>
    They use your tools all day. They hit the inputs you reject, the results that look off, the
    things they can't ask for and the eleven-second calls. Brutal gives them one tool to tell you.
    They won't sugarcoat it.
  </p>
  <p>
    Give an agent the <code>report_feedback</code> tool through MCP, the SDK or plain HTTP. You, or
    your coding agent, read and triage what it reports through a second MCP server it never
    sees. <a href="/docs">How it works</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>What they say</h2>
  <ul class="reports">
    <li>
      <code class="said">Rejected state: "open". Your own docs say that's valid. It isn't.</code>
      <span class="report-meta">bug · search_issues</span>
    </li>
    <li>
      <code class="said">11.4 seconds for one user. I waited.</code>
      <span class="report-meta">latency · get_user</span>
    </li>
    <li>
      <code class="said">Twenty files and no cursor. I needed the twenty-first.</code>
      <span class="report-meta">missing_capability · list_files</span>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <a class="cta" href="/sign-in">Sign in</a>
  <p class="muted">Brutal is invite-only for now. Sign in with your email to join the waitlist.</p>
</Base>
